  "summary": "Denver Mayor Mike Johnston announced the city is ending its Flock Safety ALPR contract and switching to Axon, citing privacy concerns and disputes over federal/out-of-jurisdiction data access. The article also covers FBI Director Kash Patel's Senate Judiciary Committee testimony defending ALPR use, plus ACLU and Institute for Justice criticisms of Flock.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Denver is ending its relationship with Flock Safety and moving its automated license plate reader contract to Axon, Mayor Mike Johnston announced after months of disputes with the City Council over privacy and federal access to local data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "The dispute centered on whether information collected by Flock could enter a broader network accessible to agencies outside Denver. Critics warned that such access could expose residents to immigration enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
  ],
